# Ocentra Parent Domain Boundaries

Shared schema truth lives in `@ocentra-parent/schema-domain` for TypeScript and
`crates/agent-protocol` for Rust, not in app code or peer domain packages.

## TypeScript Rules

- Use Effect Schema for runtime validation.
- Do not add Zod.
- Do not create manual `string & { readonly __brand: ... }` aliases.
- Use Effect Schema brands and decode helpers.
- Keep external input as `unknown` until parsed.
- Do not annotate app/runtime values as raw `string` when a domain brand exists.
- Do not place runtime text, route ids, event names, field names, or endpoint paths in app source.

## Package Ownership

| Package | Owns |
| --- | --- |
| `@ocentra-parent/schema-domain` | all canonical TypeScript runtime schemas, Effect Schema helpers, branded decode helpers, and shared contract parsers organized by domain folder |
| `@ocentra-parent/endpoint-domain` | endpoint paths, route ids, headers, query brands |
| `@ocentra-parent/agent-protocol-domain` | transport adapters, protocol mapping helpers, and consumer-facing parsers built from canonical contracts |
| `@ocentra-parent/text-domain` | schema-backed display text tokens |
| `@ocentra-parent/portal-domain` | portal route ids, DOM ids, dev command descriptors |
| `@ocentra-parent/logging-domain` | structured log/redaction helpers and log composition built from canonical contracts |
| `@ocentra-parent/parent-domain` | family, parent, child, and device business logic, projections, and helpers built from canonical contracts |
| `@ocentra-parent/activity-domain` | activity mapping, aggregation, projections, and helpers built from canonical contracts |

TypeScript rule of record:

- No package other than `@ocentra-parent/schema-domain` may own a runtime
  schema, branded value parser, or contract shape that crosses a package
  boundary.
- Domain packages may keep projection or adapter-local helpers, but they must
  import canonical contracts instead of defining peer-owned schema authorities.
- If two TypeScript packages or one TypeScript package and one Rust boundary
  need the same shape, promote it into `@ocentra-parent/schema-domain` first.

## Rust Rules

- Runtime strings live in `crates/agent-protocol` constants.
- Serde structs for shared protocol or wire contracts live in
  `crates/agent-protocol`.
- The Rust service should consume protocol constants and structs, not invent local strings.
- Platform-neutral concepts belong outside Windows-specific modules.
- Rust mirrors of TypeScript-owned contracts must preserve the exact encoded
  JSON shape: field names, discriminants, nullability, and versioning.
- Shared TS/Rust contracts must be guarded by fixture, schema-generation, or
  drift-check coverage so the two owners cannot silently diverge.

## Change Order

1. Add or update the canonical TypeScript contract in
   `@ocentra-parent/schema-domain`.
2. Add or update parser/brand tests plus shared fixture or drift-check
   coverage.
3. Mirror into `crates/agent-protocol` if the Rust service crosses the
   boundary.
4. Add or update Rust-side parity coverage for the mirrored contract.
5. Update package, portal, and service consumers.
6. Run the validation gate.
